The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
		if (!arvif->is_created)
			continue;
```
Reason: When an arvif is initialized but not created (`is_created` is false), the removal loop skips it without calling `ath12k_mac_unassign_link_vif()`. This leaves a stale mapping in `ahvif->link[link_id]`, causing a WARN_ON when a new arvif with the same link id is later initialized.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
		if (!arvif->is_created) {
			ath12k_mac_unassign_link_vif(arvif);
			continue;
		}
```
Reason: By calling `ath12k_mac_unassign_link_vif(arvif)` before continuing, the stale link mapping is properly cleared. This ensures that when a new arvif with the same link id is created, no stale reference remains, preventing the WARN_ON.

